he folders and files that take up the most space in MacReviver?\nHow do I use Disk Usage to find the folders and files that take up the most space in MacReviver?\nThe Disk Usage feature gathers statistics on all the folders on your Mac, and tells you which folders take up the most space. As you click through folders, each subfolder will also be sorted by space. You can also remove any folder or file from this screen.\nTo use Disk Usage:\nLaunch MacReviver.\nClick\nDisk Usage\n.\nClick\nScan\n.\nThe folders will be color coded by size. Red folders and files take up the most space within a particular folder, and green takes up the least space.\nClick the arrow to view subfolders, which are similarly color coded.\nSelect any folder or file, and click\nRemove\nto delete it.\nSorry this did not help. What problem are you experiencing?\nGreat! Thanks for the feedback.\nDid this answer help?\nYes\nNo\nSearch existing questions\nSimilar articles\nHow do I use Quick Cleanup to clean unnecessary files in MacReviver?\nHow do I use Duplicates Finder to remove duplicate files in MacReviver?\nHow do I use Files Finder to find large files, or any files, in MacReviver?\nHow do I use Junk File Cleaner to remove the trash and temporary files in MacReviver?\nHow do I use the backup function of MacReviver?\nQuick Help\nLost Your License Key\nDownload Products\nAccess Your Account\nOrder Status and More\ncontact reviversoft Support\nContact one of our friendly support team members for a quick response.\nContact support\nCompany\n|\nPartners\n|\nEULA\n|\nLegal Notice\n|\nDo Not Sell/Share My Info\n|\nManage My Cookies\nCopyright \u00a9 2026 Corel Corporation. All rights reserved.\nTerms Of Use\n|\nPrivacy\n|\nCookies\nfollow us\nEdit translation\nMachine translation (Google):\nLoading...\nCopy to editor\nor\nCancel",
